  "summary_en": "Tennessee bill (HB 591/SB 796), the \"Freedom from Unwarranted Surveillance Act\", banning law enforcement use of drones to gather evidence or information, with exceptions for warrants, terrorism threats, and imminent danger. It provides a civil action and evidence exclusion for violations.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Law enforcement agencies may not use drones to gather evidence or information.",
   "Exceptions: DHS-determined terrorist threat, judicial search warrant, or reasonable suspicion of imminent danger to life.",
   "Aggrieved parties may bring civil actions against agencies.",
   "Evidence obtained in violation is inadmissible in criminal prosecutions.",
   "Proposed effective date July 1, 2013."
  ],
